98} :answer-field/id #uuid "19bef9f2-14bf-5988-884b-2c3e717c03e5" :answer-field/key "$K(x,y,z)=x\\,i-y\\,j+z\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438828}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2d1a20d-340e-5980-ad18-92b97e0270ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-122465" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $G(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $H(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$; $H(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{xy}\\,j$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9db2c395-ec42-5ded-b118-40b7f641733e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437612} {:answer/id #uuid "416808ed-a781-5b4b-95e5-19a652e061b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "416808ed-a781-5b4b-95e5-19a652e061b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437613} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3b88c55-88f1-525f-b310-4ec0ae74fb86" :answer-field/key "$P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438835} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b870f025-7855-54e1-ba52-ff6dc5d12029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437614} {:answer/id #uuid "272a82e6-92c9-5b61-b5b0-91bb28d461e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b870f025-7855-54e1-ba52-ff6dc5d12029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437614} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd800195-cb3a-5cb6-83d8-4a289879ed7b" :answer-field/key "$Q(x,y,z)$ $=y\\,i$ $-xy\\,j$ $+(z+1)\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d35aa822-dcce-5b60-823d-bc8fd4d47fd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437616} {:answer/id #uuid "57ad27bc-d96f-5039-a317-bdadedc1b542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d35aa822-dcce-5b60-823d-bc8fd4d47fd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437616} :answer-field/id #uuid "91b9cc2d-8a9d-5c85-8be1-4e96ec3dbdef" :answer-field/key "$R(t)=(t+1)\\,i-(3t-1)\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438837}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7b23ed53-bb63-5272-af53-a6429d08e4c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-122643" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $R(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256685 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5dfdb090-b6f2-5639-aede-69a2ab60459d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437618} {:answer/id #uuid "8709f1c4-65e1-54b0-9d7e-fb1cb2bfbedf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8709f1c4-65e1-54b0-9d7e-fb1cb2bfbedf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437619} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8671b01-0de0-54e6-81e3-d9dce3d551cb" :answer-field/key "$U(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x+2},\\sqrt{x-y}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f49f49bb-0589-51e3-8307-793ca10c0906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437620} {:answer/id #uuid "e78b01f6-8039-5eb5-a36a-b79ac0375eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e78b01f6-8039-5eb5-a36a-b79ac0375eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437621} :answer-field/id #uuid "811ad6c5-2f4c-5371-a120-40ade9271191" :answer-field/key "$V(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},1-y⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177eaf39-4c0c-56e2-b24b-1fe2e1490f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437622} {:answer/id #uuid "3b92af76-e3cd-572a-82c2-a86f00b68ae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "177eaf39-4c0c-56e2-b24b-1fe2e1490f63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437622} :answer-field/id #uuid "1603ebdc-1768-5b01-b37c-c00c63150d1d" :answer-field/key "$W(x,y,z)=⟨x,-y,-z⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438840}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82c19ae8-c5db-5680-ac18-77dd108b7959" :question/math-academy-id "q-122650" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne -2,\\,x-y\\ge 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $W(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $U(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x+2},\\sqrt{x-y}⟩$; $V(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},1-y⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a345da55-40a0-58c5-bd97-11513a3c18ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437624} {:answer/id #uuid "91b6594a-7883-5a7f-8bd5-9117346c6a52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :