th-academy-id "q-122653" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A(x,y)$ $=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "719148a4-d796-5d0f-bf37-0acb3355c237" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437642} {:answer/id #uuid "eba23c1d-3faf-5e1e-a91b-717c3d32e34d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eba23c1d-3faf-5e1e-a91b-717c3d32e34d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437643} :answer-field/id #uuid "4df690b3-4439-5e28-93c0-aefae7e9325b" :answer-field/key "$U(x,y)=⟨(x+2){e}^{y},\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x-y}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438850} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f151183d-0ec4-55fd-8ac2-5a941eb7fbb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437644} {:answer/id #uuid "c063cfd4-fff8-5a50-8d56-88acaeadffe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f151183d-0ec4-55fd-8ac2-5a941eb7fbb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437644} :answer-field/id #uuid "75092fdd-a6da-542b-8e4b-55dd63863ac1" :answer-field/key "$V(x,y,z)=⟨5,{x}^{3}y,1-{y}^{3}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438851} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a91aca-2e42-57f0-a9b8-8c67da63bfa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437646} {:answer/id #uuid "34d621d2-368f-51fa-b847-821e2249a80d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34d621d2-368f-51fa-b847-821e2249a80d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437647} :answer-field/id #uuid "993bc041-4fb8-52cb-aed9-367ffe93abcb" :answer-field/key "$W(x,y)=⟨x-3{y}^{2},2-y⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438852}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f63ae22-12f3-552d-bede-acf1007c6564" :question/math-academy-id "q-122678" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne y}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $U(x,y)=⟨(x+2){e}^{y},\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x-y}⟩$; $W(x,y)=⟨x-3{y}^{2},2-y⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380657 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "162499c9-d211-5946-8b2e-c019541c3034" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437606} {:answer/id #uuid "96e0faf2-fb61-5450-8ad0-ff90febe7fb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96e0faf2-fb61-5450-8ad0-ff90febe7fb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437607} :answer-field/id #uuid "428e492b-b338-505d-b794-6840361998af" :answer-field/key "$G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4078c42f-287d-5b03-8583-af065de039c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437608} {:answer/id #uuid "b2eb56cf-3f62-5c54-b952-b89ebe56b894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4078c42f-287d-5b03-8583-af065de039c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437608} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc0a8721-d4c0-531c-850b-a28514d4f48c" :answer-field/key "$H(t)=\\sqrt{t}\\,i+t{e}^{t}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24149d6d-29cf-587b-9c73-d17502c56d1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437610} {:answer/id #uuid "642982e1-2a9a-5105-be2e-a1a9730e6358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24149d6d-29cf-587b-9c73-d17502c56d1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437610} :answer-field/id #uuid "571b08b4-5fa1-5191-8779-09ec9667116b" :answer-field/key "$K(x,y,z)=2x\\,i+y\\,j-3z\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438834}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1de1af2b-64e8-50cf-80c9-f414743fe7ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-122641" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $G(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $H(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1447082-f4e8-5788-a80e-d8c2f8b82522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437630} {:answer/id #uuid "747beaa6-cbb1-5ab8-b6f0-aac6db2ca380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1447082-f4e8-5788-a80e-d8c2f8b82522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437630} :answer-field/id #uuid "89920c46-71c7-5175-8718-e990046088f6" :answer-field/key "$M(x,y)$ $=⟨y-{x}^{2},3x+{y}^{2},\\frac{1}{x+y}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5963b314-2add-567a-b457-6f81885a3dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437632} {:answer/id #uuid "0a97ce34-6fad-5a23-a913-7a8c54c9939c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a97ce34-6fad-5a23-a913-7a8c54c9939c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437633} :answer-field/id #uuid "121c69dd-36e1-570a-bd6d-c832cafb4cd4" :answer-field/key "$N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2852e063-18c2-5c27-805a-899fefe85cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437634} {:answer/id #uuid "2d47eb09-37b1-5b48-8d81-6237d57c3ab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2852e063-18c2-5c27-805a-899fefe85cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437634} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6caeebf-8412-599a-8bb3-625ed3e2bddb" :answer-field/key "$P(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\sqrt{1-t}\\,⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438846}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "502cb71c-02d6-5e14-a31b-2cee28a0a5ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-122656" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $M(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  ${R}^{2}$ to vectors in ${R}^{3}$ (not in ${R}^{2}$).\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $P(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ \n(not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acbf2816-9f71-5351-b1d8-a801bf30542d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437636} {:answer/id #uuid "308d0f3d-2e87-5cc6-b65f-2f83e5267801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "308d0f3d-2e87-5cc6-b65f-2f83e5267801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437637} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe68175-15ca-5f31-9cf5-5f03083fe4fb" :answer-field/key "$C(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x+y},{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0725d6f3-2622-5e9f-9c94-bfc7b72d7402" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437638} {:answer/id #uuid "81503c2a-ae1a-5a4d-882d-f15bf57c0190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81503c2a-ae1a-5a4d-882d-f15bf57c0190" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437639} :answer-field/id #uuid "920a7af7-aee4-545a-b604-ad8eca5e6e88" :answer-field/key "$D(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3}-3,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438848} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceb42624-bc8c-5336-8d28-af87d45d5914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437640} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8e9ded-65e6-530c-8fb7-a0624c962138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceb42624-bc8c-5336-8d28-af87d45d5914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437640} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a744e92-3f60-596f-918f-2e9f6b8fc76b" :answer-field/key "$E(x,y)=⟨x+1,y+2,x-y⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438849}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b352a16-fe6f-5946-bac9-7b334007947a" :question/math-academy-id "q-122675" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $D(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $E(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ to vectors in ${R}^{3}$ (not ${R}^{2}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $C(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x+y},{x}^{2}{e}^{y}⟩$; $D(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3}-3,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-y)⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45fd9da9-66ec-5c9f-bf50-20f83d472ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 175921