ficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e2a1d7f-e53f-5a9c-a708-98dd5132af11" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $H(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y>2\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $K(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $G(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $H(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-2)\\,i-{e}^{xy}\\,j$; $G(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i-{y}^{2}\\,j$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aab6b82-5473-54b2-8342-d5b12a067309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567189} {:answer/id #uuid "1a0e194e-4e46-543a-b453-b158f7199720" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aab6b82-5473-54b2-8342-d5b12a067309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567189} :answer-field/id #uuid "140553c9-c715-584b-af3a-6b6e155f93da" :answer-field/key "$Q(x,y,z)$ $=y\\,i$ $-xy\\,j$ $+(z+1)\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb25ee9-04ae-575a-9259-57c85282e565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567204} {:answer/id #uuid "9164bfd5-cb32-508b-8e82-54cd22cfb331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9164bfd5-cb32-508b-8e82-54cd22cfb331" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567213} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d59b728-8e77-50a1-b7a9-06a1db730e10" :answer-field/key "$R(t)=(t+1)\\,i-(3t-1)\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567205} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f52addd-f29a-5307-ae63-57aeb5e24897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567196} {:answer/id #uuid "bf72c3b5-0933-59e6-8af7-64086a0a9c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567221}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f52addd-f29a-5307-ae63-57aeb5e24897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567196} :answer-field/id #uuid "a78558c4-f036-560a-9350-e3c6ca01857c" :answer-field/key "$P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567218}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30a80a69-f783-54d8-ab59-5af7c2f92b56" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne -4\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $R(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{(x+4)^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f564c027-fe6e-57d9-a714-0695c3318f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567235} {:answer/id #uuid "f91c6a42-c1ac-5529-a9f6-7a1965c45958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f564c027-fe6e-57d9-a714-0695c3318f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567235} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ec835d2-9c51-51a2-89e9-974324e8cc7d" :answer-field/key "$V(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},1-y⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567203} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5b33e90-1466-5240-a67e-a0c0e98ce9bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567225} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9fd356-b1cc-55c6-959b-beb5488e380a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee9fd356-b1cc-55c6-959b-beb5488e380a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567233} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0b57d94-202b-5646-ba11-25ee2943d2df" :answer-field/key "$W(x,y,z)=⟨x,-y,-z⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42696c72-5443-560e-83aa-8ffbba82a1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567200} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2ef185-0854-5ff5-bb45-ebf9ffcd2a5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee2ef185-0854-5ff5-bb45-ebf9ffcd2a5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567232} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf0b982b-2cb4-5648-b036-aebfb29a4068" :answer-field/key "$U(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x-1},\\sqrt{x-y}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567220}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c84dc6d-f3c5-526f-a4f4-5ad6cd0c3bce" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $W(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $U(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 1,\\,x-y\\ge 0\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $V(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},1-y⟩$; $U(x,y)=⟨\\frac{1}{x-1},\\sqrt{x-y}⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c919761a-b785-5467-9d53-ffdebf92193b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567223} {:answer/id #uuid "f8e23ac4-649f-541d-bc51-71ecb623818b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c919761a-b785-5467-9d53-ffdebf92193b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567223} :answer-field/id #uuid "18ec5692-c9ef-5f0c-a652-876b5d6fbb3f" :answer-field/key "$B(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,3{y}^{3},{z}^{5}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e2ffb53-48eb-5a77-9716-29f4fd2040fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567199} {:answer/id #uuid "da47e72c-dc30-5c30-ae3b-d7a7f95b1d80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e2ffb53-48eb-5a77-9716-29f4fd2040fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567199} :answer-field/id #uuid "852bf52c-3a7e-53ad-b9fa-453243fd2c19" :answer-field/key "$A(x,y)$ $=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+1)⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567209} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a259de5-9796-55c9-8079-35fabc03dd3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567198} {:answer/id #uuid "945f5c81-d864-5180-9be8-3393a76465b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a259de5-9796-55c9-8079-35fabc03dd3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567198} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b10bdf6-7c39-5c1b-8df6-83ff198409aa" :answer-field/key "$C(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},{e}^{t-1}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567215}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de33a652-95eb-51a9-8764-ce6e9dad4ffc" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>-1\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A(x,y)$ $=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+1)⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567231 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e216b54-3105-5bba-8558-960e7437f115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567190} {:answer/id #uuid "79c44a8f-9149-58c3-bc99-49bc40412f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79c44a8f-9149-58c3-bc99-49bc40412f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567206} :answer-field/id #uuid "03913288-f4c8-5caa-b009-cf8b543f4718" :answer-field/key "$C(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},{e}^{t-1}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d70cf5a4-bb36-520b-8a7c-e89b04e60e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567226} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a02875-02cc-550f-9d11-9ae466df6873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d70cf5a4-bb36-520b-8a7c-e89b04e60e3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567226} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf0499ee-048f-5d24-8ef1-b8b998c793c5" :answer-field/key "$B(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,3{y}^{3},{z}^{5}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b1d6ecb-47c4-5b01-818c-0431e0dee59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567194} {:answer/id #uuid "43a221f3-b2b9-5ba0-a8ae-f914d4b64fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b1d6ecb-47c4-5b01-818c-0431e0dee59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567194} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2875da9-e1ba-58d5-8b5a-07575bdaecab" :answer-field/key "$A(x,y)$ $=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+4)⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186567234}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e81f7559-db38-57e6-b2e9-f6d8f3a3c157" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>-4\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A(x,y)$ $=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+4)⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63d03417-eb5c-556b-8e3e-71f501713090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707356} {:answer/id #uuid "f11bd925-496b-5f6a-b477-10eaa4830f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f11bd925-496b-5f6a-b477-10eaa4830f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707374} :answer-field/id #uuid "3db612dd-1e25-53aa-8674-179a5112bcc6" :answer-field/key "$C(x,y)=x^2+y^2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c7d1054-bb58-553e-a857-862e42bdd13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707349} {:answer/id #uuid "f4dc0638-cd33-51ef-b54c-bddf9cda81b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c7d1054-bb58-553e-a857-862e42bdd13f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707349} :answer-field/id #uuid "4497d788-bbc3-52b0-bca2-0a22fc0ec156" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf A(x,y,z)=\\langle y,x-y\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180f1a75-b8b5-509a-923d-fb66f0e760d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707346} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7ddf4c-c9cc-59f9-bce7-aa072a75f6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb7ddf4c-c9cc-59f9-bce7-aa072a75f6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707370} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eb2ed84-2b20-5cec-9d64-89672056972d" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf B(u,v)=\\langle u^2,0\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707360}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248652e3-f6c5-5073-aae7-554bf75b40eb" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nEach input coordinate ranges independently over $\\mathbb R$." :question/worked-solution "The input space is determined by the declared input coordinates, even if a coordinate does not appear in the formula. The output must be a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf A$ returns a vector with two components, but its input is a triple $(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3$. Not using $z$ does not change that input space. Therefore $\\mathbf A$ is not a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf B$ takes the planar point $(u,v)$ to the planar vector $\\langle u^2,0\\rangle$. Both components are real for all $(u,v)\\in\\mathbb R^2$. The second component may be zero, and the formula need not depend on both input coordinates. Thus $\\mathbf B$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $C$ takes planar inputs but returns a scalar, not a planar vector. For example, $C(1,2)=5$, not a vector with two components. It is a scalar field.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf B$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707357 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8676fb6b-aad9-5815-b176-bd99080aad80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707359} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c5b3f7-82d4-50cc-b11a-c07f8066c621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3c5b3f7-82d4-50cc-b11a-c07f8066c621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707372} :answer-field/id #uuid "59e6458e-cb93-5b4c-b07e-f8691c32c057" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf H(t)=(t+1)\\,\\mathbf i+t^2\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707354} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7651a6b1-4b06-5c1f-8652-a982b6598b61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707358} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c76ccd-64b2-5506-a2e0-f154c586dc71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4c76ccd-64b2-5506-a2e0-f154c586dc71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707366} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b7ff29-04d7-51a4-9458-73f36041552c" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\sqrt{x+1}\\,\\mathbf i+(x-y)\\,\\mathbf j$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e3f6f8-5899-5be8-aa15-012c72bbc420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707348} {:answer/id #uuid "5277db7d-a45e-56d4-902c-8d3940198a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30e3f6f8-5899-5be8-aa15-012c72bbc420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707348} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0c59fe5-d8e7-505d-8886-f140971d71d8" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf G(x,y,z)=y\\,\\mathbf i-x\\,\\mathbf j+z\\,\\mathbf k$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707373}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "64bdbefc-9ee8-51e3-93c0-11b6364f721e" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply.\n\nA vector field assigns a vector in $\\mathbb R^2$ to each point of a subset of $\\mathbb R^2$. A formula may have a restricted natural domain." :question/worked-solution "Check both the input points and the output vectors.\n\n- $\\mathbf F$ takes planar input points and returns planar vectors. Its square root is real when $x\\geq -1$, so it is defined on the subset\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x\\geq -1\\}.\n$$\n\nA domain smaller than the whole plane is allowed. Thus $\\mathbf F$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf G$ takes points in $\\mathbb R^3$ and returns vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$. It is a three-dimensional vector field, not a vector field on $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\n- $\\mathbf H$ returns planar vectors, but its input is a single real parameter $t$. It describes a parametrized curve, not a vector field with planar inputs.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf F$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ef3ab76-c3c5-5cfc-8124-aa7a0267a79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707361} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f08462-ccbc-535b-97a3-9347b2f80a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ef3ab76-c3c5-5cfc-8124-aa7a0267a79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707361} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb97b75-254b-56a7-8735-318c6822de8b" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf Q(u,v)=\\sqrt{u-v}\\,\\mathbf i+\\ln(u+v)\\,\\mathbf j$, on $T$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af03f5c8-10cd-54d0-98db-b966d2bae7d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707363} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e8329c-08d8-5aa1-b4fe-7d7e90f98af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2e8329c-08d8-5aa1-b4fe-7d7e90f98af4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707365} :answer-field/id #uuid "b14b1b08-ab1d-5346-b5f0-37774250ee36" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf P(x,y)=\\sqrt{x-y}\\,\\mathbf i+\\ln(x+y)\\,\\mathbf j$, on $S$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a13252a-67f4-5327-9201-f08da4b2b6d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707355} {:answer/id #uuid "b86717a0-cd9d-5111-85a4-817c3ea37be2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b86717a0-cd9d-5111-85a4-817c3ea37be2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707368} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbe2ec6f-65c8-5920-b355-107d1da50fc8" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbf R(s,t)=\\sin s\\,\\mathbf i$, on $\\mathbb R^2$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707371}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b6d5ec1a-a97b-54c7-bc35-cc60d1536152" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their entire stated domains? Select all that apply. Keep each stated domain unchanged.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x\\geq y\\}.\n$$\n\n$$\nT=\\{(u,v)\\in\\mathbb R^2:u\\geq v,\\ u+v>0\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Each candidate uses planar input points. Check that its formula gives a real planar vector at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- For $\\mathbf P$, the condition $x\\geq y$ makes $\\sqrt{x-y}$ real, but it does not guarantee $x+y>0$. For example, $(0,0)\\in S$, yet $\\ln(0)$ is undefined. Thus the formula does not define a vector field on all of $S$. It would work on a smaller domain, but that is not the domain stated in the question.\n\n- For $\\mathbf Q$, every $(u,v)\\in T$ satisfies both $u-v\\geq 0$ and $u+v>0$. Therefore both components are real at every point of $T$, including the allowed boundary $u=v>0$. Its outputs are planar vectors, so $\\mathbf Q$ is a vector field on the stated domain $T$.\n\n- The missing $\\mathbf j$ term in $\\mathbf R$ has coefficient zero:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(s,t)=\\sin s\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\sin s,0\\rangle.\n$$\n\nThis is a planar vector for every planar input $(s,t)$. Independence from $t$ does not turn a two-input function into a one-input function. Hence $\\mathbf R$ is a vector field on all of $\\mathbb R^2$.\n\nSelect $\\mathbf Q$ and $\\mathbf R$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07250558-c46d-5dc0-aae7-2b4c74b870d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707475} {:answer/id #uuid "c5113b47-6c5d-5aee-a8f6-ed1202372083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07250558-c46d-5dc0-aae7-2b4c74b870d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707475} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc85fe1e-8e16-5eed-83b3-a583d02bb24b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707512} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "776a362e-5a5d-5402-9735-b9408b301b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707491} {:answer/id #uuid "887d6ab8-34bd-514d-9d34-35e11bb57002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "887d6ab8-34bd-514d-9d34-35e11bb57002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707496} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd76a44a-4fca-58f7-b239-543bd79fbe87" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab46545-0f01-5656-9a5f-c139d7bf503b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707477} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7b5a55-f8a3-5ff0-99e4-a0d58d6f7dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab46545-0f01-5656-9a5f-c139d7bf503b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707477} :answer-field/id #uuid "f21d3b70-33af-5145-bdc6-3eab6b1abfe2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1e324553-d08f-5dbc-b9fd-80a83282ecb8" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $G(x,y)=\\ln(x+2)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+2>0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y+1},\\ln(x+y+3)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y+1\\geq0,\\ x+y+3\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $V(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x+2},\\sqrt{y+1}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+2\\geq0,\\ y+1\\geq0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $G$ The components require $x+2>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x+2)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x+2),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $F$ The components require $x-y+1\\geq0,\\ x+y+3>0$. The point $(-2,-1)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\ln(0)$; the logarithm is undefined. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **III.** $V$ The components require $x+2\\ne0,\\ y+1\\geq0$. The point $(-2,0)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $1/0$; the reciprocal is undefined. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\nSelect I only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707494 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "482d1d74-2f4a-5ab9-9281-951a0af4e8b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707483} {:answer/id #uuid "92d5b50d-f72c-5d26-b2a8-0a1c93248ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d5b50d-f72c-5d26-b2a8-0a1c93248ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707500} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d05b28-cad7-5a10-9036-e05c69e9af36" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7506b157-34f1-55ba-b69d-6943fbc2dca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707490} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8d44b7-53a4-5eab-9e89-5f8432cbb1b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7506b157-34f1-55ba-b69d-6943fbc2dca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707490} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f683d51-6023-5e35-bedf-9fdbd5cbc691" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3fe546e-4f7b-527d-8b9a-81b00def49a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707519} {:answer/id #uuid "f8fc23b9-d097-53c0-9211-d21779680509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8fc23b9-d097-53c0-9211-d21779680509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707524} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded1cc39-82fa-5ad4-9d02-deb3007dfc89" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707516}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "84ce4948-b314-559d-b491-894660b2cd10" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $K(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y-1},\\ln(x+y-1)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y-1\\geq-1,\\ x+y-1>0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $E(x,y)=\\ln(x-1)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-1\\geq1\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $B(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x-1},\\sqrt{y}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-1\\ne0,\\ y\\geq0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $K$ The components require $x-y-1\\geq0,\\ x+y-1>0$. The point $(1,1)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\sqrt{-1}$; the square root is not real. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **II.** $E$ The components require $x-1>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x-1)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x-1),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **III.** $B$ The components require $x-1\\ne0,\\ y\\geq0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The square-root boundary $y=0$ is allowed when $x-1\\ne0$.  The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\nSelect II, III only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c439e96-0377-50d4-a7af-4895e546b673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707489} {:answer/id #uuid "df0bf835-376a-5025-8812-2c80f4fd9c38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c439e96-0377-50d4-a7af-4895e546b673" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707489} :answer-field/id #uuid "88ea6a6c-91a0-54bc-b703-cb6847059b9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707497} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "504b9475-89dd-5a30-90c3-f87bb65635cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707485} {:answer/id #uuid "abcaaaa9-c1ee-563d-a4a7-81074edda576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abcaaaa9-c1ee-563d-a4a7-81074edda576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707506} :answer-field/id #uuid "b33167b7-c792-5521-b8b6-c060924b0d76" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707507} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b225ad2-8aed-5a8a-9ea7-737b8662460e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707488} {:answer/id #uuid "da970778-204d-582c-9661-25ade4a1f096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b225ad2-8aed-5a8a-9ea7-737b8662460e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707488} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6f5f3a7-517a-5540-8ea6-e9d6962644ff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707523}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "85c4ad5f-229c-59e7-b9e8-e849af9f5efb" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $B(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x-2},\\sqrt{y-3}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\ne0,\\ y-3\\geq-1\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $M(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y+1},\\ln(x+y-5)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y+1\\geq-1,\\ x+y-5>0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $J(x,y)=\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\geq1\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $B$ The components require $x-2\\ne0,\\ y-3\\geq0$. The point $(3,2)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\sqrt{-1}$; the square root is not real. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **II.** $M$ The components require $x-y+1\\geq0,\\ x+y-5>0$. The point $(2,4)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\sqrt{-1}$; the square root is not real. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **III.** $J$ The components require $x-2>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x-2),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\nSelect III only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer