checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707515}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c63a2d70-cbd3-5739-9fa6-3418fa252c08" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $D(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x-2},\\sqrt{y-2}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\ne0,\\ y-2\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $F(x,y)=\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-2\\geq0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $N(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y},\\ln(x+y-4)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y\\geq0,\\ x+y-4>0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $D$ The components require $x-2\\ne0,\\ y-2\\geq0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The square-root boundary $y-2=0$ is allowed when $x-2\\ne0$.  The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $F$ The components require $x-2>0$. The point $(2,2)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $\\ln(0)$; the logarithm is undefined. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x-2)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x-2),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\n- **III.** $N$ The components require $x-y\\geq0,\\ x+y-4>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The boundary $x-2=y-2>0$ is allowed. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\nSelect I, III only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7edbcea0-a4e4-5b9a-abe8-777381fee67c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1