e2ee" :question/problem "Which formulas define vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$ on their **entire stated domains**? Select all that apply. Keep every stated domain unchanged. The symbols $\\mathbf i,\\mathbf j$ are the planar unit vectors.\n\n- **I.** $T(x,y)=\\langle\\sqrt{x-y+6},\\ln(x+y)\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x-y+6\\geq0,\\ x+y>0\\}$.\n\n- **II.** $M(x,y)=\\ln(x+3)\\,\\mathbf i$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+3>0\\}$.\n\n- **III.** $J(x,y)=\\langle\\frac{1}{x+3},\\sqrt{y-3}\\rangle$ on $\\{(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2:x+3\\geq0,\\ y-3\\geq0\\}$." :question/worked-solution "Check planar inputs and outputs, then test whether the formula is real and defined at every point of the stated domain.\n\n- **I.** $T$ The components require $x-y+6\\geq0,\\ x+y>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The boundary $x+3=y-3>0$ is allowed. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $M$ The components require $x+3>0$. Every point in the stated domain satisfies these conditions. The omitted planar component is zero: $\\ln(x+3)\\,\\mathbf i+0\\,\\mathbf j=\\langle\\ln(x+3),0\\rangle$. Its output is still planar. The inputs and outputs are planar, so select this function.\n\n- **III.** $J$ The components require $x+3\\ne0,\\ y-3\\geq0$. The point $(-3,4)$ lies in the stated domain, but gives $1/0$; the reciprocal is undefined. The formula therefore fails on the entire stated domain. Do not select this function; shrinking the domain is not allowed in this question.\n\nSelect I, II only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d472eed-f8d5-5ee1-9db7-ccd243145067" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707527} {:answer/id #uuid "14f49d01-9486-5e0b-8026-e0a57a22b0fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14f49d01-9486-5e0b-8026-e0a57a22b0fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707530} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc538ee-e54b-52e6-bbbe-e548ffff4ef2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22201626-0d65-5fb0-8e7f-a5c6db38b7c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707532} {:answer/id #uuid "ee630744-08fb-5098-b051-3d0c2d1b3a4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22201626-0d65-5fb0-8e7f-a5c6db38b7c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707532} :answer-field/id #uuid "9390f336-9f3b-5b94-a124-ab73085df8f7" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707548} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5048a3e8-9a7c-531d-8409-ee8d0b2b37e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707539} {:answer/id #uuid "7627e420-8cf7-5cc7-a547-e2aa1271d5fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5048a3e8-9a7c-531d-8409-ee8d0b2b37e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707539} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3df1e7e-d2ef-5e0c-9b14-53cd99b9c8be" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707561}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26d1b88a-fd6c-549a-8858-e6e5e3ae5994" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^2$? Select all that apply. Use each function's declared input coordinates and its natural real domain.\n\n- **I.** $Z(x,y)=(\\frac{1}{(x+2)})\\,\\mathbf i+(0)\\,\\mathbf j$\n\n- **II.** $S(x,y)=\\frac{1}{(x+2)}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)}$\n\n- **III.** $A(x,y)=\\langle (x+2)^2,(x+2)^2\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "Check the input dimension and output dimension.\n\n- **I.** $Z$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x+2)\\ne 0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $S$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a scalar. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x+2)\\ne 0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. The input and output are not both two-dimensional, so do not select this function.\n\n- **III.** $A$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. All components are real on $\\mathbb R^2$. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\nSelect I, III only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "463f9121-f892-55ea-8855-64ab6be167bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707538} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfc7e87-b22a-55a0-bf9a-9a021779e76f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccfc7e87-b22a-55a0-bf9a-9a021779e76f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707558} :answer-field/id #uuid "029f9108-2cca-5ec6-8e3b-57e798b4508a" :answer-field/key "I