d output dimension.\n\n- **I.** $S$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x+1)>0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\n- **II.** $E$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 3 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x+1)>0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. The input and output are not both two-dimensional, so do not select this function.\n\n- **III.** $C$ takes 3 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. All components are real on $\\mathbb R^3$. The input and output are not both two-dimensional, so do not select this function.\n\nSelect I only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707562 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f6dfd85-07b3-5d70-9266-65550791dff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707536} {:answer/id #uuid "89f5ad3d-88c0-5eb0-a420-f9a51f18676d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f6dfd85-07b3-5d70-9266-65550791dff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707536} :answer-field/id #uuid "357985f3-1ac7-587a-bd10-beaa437e5d7f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b81ff8f-267c-5fde-9c13-332e03