he input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(t)\\in \\mathbb R^1:(t-2)\\geq 0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. The input and output are not both two-dimensional, so do not select this function.\n\n- **II.** $F$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x-2)>0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\n- **III.** $T$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 3 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:(x-2)>0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. The input and output are not both two-dimensional, so do not select this function.\n\nSelect II only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186707564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45dc2808-5c9b-55a6-baf3-ebefe7745b8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707537} {:answer/id #uuid "ab666c46-dad4-53b0-8e87-7c5a9ad4ce89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab666c46-dad4-53b0-8e87-7c5a9ad4ce89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707553} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fce2b1e-157e-5ef3-9d8e-7441d26aae80" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186707529} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f680cd2-8b2e-59a4-8a2f-df7c5f3befe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} 