nents are real on $\\mathbb R^1$. The input and output are not both two-dimensional, so do not select this function.\n\n- **II.** $D$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. Its natural real domain is $\\{(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2:x\\geq 0\\}$, which is nonempty. A restricted natural domain is allowed. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\n- **III.** $F$ takes 2 input coordinates and returns a vector with 2 components. The declared input list determines the input dimension, even when a coordinate is unused; a zero output coordinate still counts. All components are real on $\\mathbb R^2$. Both dimensions are two, so select this function.\n\nSelect II, III only."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions"}]}
